          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تطلب — taṭallaba — \"to require\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "يتطلب هذا العمل صبرا كبيرا. yataṭallabu hādhā al-ʿamal ṣabran kabīran. This work requires great patience."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: يتطلب, yataṭallab."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تطلب (taṭallaba) is built on the native Arabic root ṭ-l-b, \"to seek, to ask for\" (Lane). It is Form V, to seek a thing again and again: to call for, to require."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
